  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A doubling means the population changes from 12 to\n\n\\[\n2(12)=24.\n\\]\n\nThe increase is\n\n\\[\n24-12=12.\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population, the percentage increase is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase when the population doubles is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}.\n\\]\n\n(Under the separate rule that the population triples each month, the actual one-month increase would instead be \\(200\\%\\).)",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. The number of students on campus doubles at the end of every month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with 12 students, doubling at the end of the month gives\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24 \\text{ students}.\n\\]\n\nThe increase is\n\n\\[\n24-12=12 \\text{ students}.\n\\]\n\nThe percentage increase relative to the original population is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. There are 10 students on campus at the beginning of the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With 10 students initially, doubling gives\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2=20.\n\\]\n\nThe increase is\n\n\\[\n20-10=10.\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the student population is multiplied by 2 after each completed month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "After each completed month, the population is multiplied by \\(2\\). Starting with \\(10\\) students:\n\n\\[\n10 \\longrightarrow 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is \\(20-10=10\\) students. Relative to the original population:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase each month is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with \\(10\\) students and doubling after each completed month:\n\n- After 1 month: \\(10 \\times 2=20\\)\n- After 2 months: \\(20 \\times 2=40\\)\n- After 3 months: \\(40 \\times 2=80\\)\n\nEquivalently,\n\n\\[\n10\\cdot 2^3=80.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A doubling means multiplying the current population by \\(2\\). Starting with \\(10\\) students:\n\n\\[\n10 \\xrightarrow{\\text{1 month}} 20\n\\xrightarrow{\\text{2 months}} 40\n\\xrightarrow{\\text{3 months}} 80.\n\\]\n\nEquivalently,\n\n\\[\n10\\cdot 2^3=80.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, after three completed months, there will be\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "There are 5 completed months from the beginning of the year through the end of May. The population doubles each month:\n\n\\[\n10\\cdot 2^5=10\\cdot 32=320\n\\]\n\nSo, by the end of May, there are 320 students. The number of additional students beyond the original 10 is\n\n\\[\n320-10=310.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{310\\text{ additional students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
